1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,774
Monthly rent is posted on its own.

2
00:00:02,774 --> 00:00:06,738
Every night, each month that has ended
moves from Advance

3
00:00:06,738 --> 00:00:10,702
Rent to Rental Income, as one journal for
each contract.

4
00:00:10,702 --> 00:00:13,872
On Fatima Al Zaabi's contract for A-102,
July

5
00:00:13,872 --> 00:00:17,043
and August are Posted, each with its
journal.

6
00:00:17,043 --> 00:00:20,214
September has ended, but it is still
Planned.

7
00:00:20,214 --> 00:00:22,592
To see everything that is waiting,

8
00:00:22,592 --> 00:00:24,574
open Accounting, then Month-end
recognition.

9
00:00:24,574 --> 00:00:28,141
The warning says ten ended months,
87,369.90 in all,

10
00:00:28,141 --> 00:00:31,709
are not recognised yet, the oldest ending
in January.

11
00:00:31,709 --> 00:00:35,672
The list shows them by building: Fatima's
September, and nine

12
00:00:35,672 --> 00:00:39,636
months of Sara Mansour's contract for
M-1501, which was posted

13
00:00:39,636 --> 00:00:43,599
in late September for a term that began in
January.

14
00:00:43,599 --> 00:00:48,355
The To date is already the end of last
month, the thirtieth

15
00:00:48,355 --> 00:00:52,715
of September: a month that has not ended
is never recognised.

16
00:00:52,715 --> 00:00:56,679
Select Preview: ten periods, 87,369.90,
and nothing is written yet.

17
00:00:56,679 --> 00:00:59,057
Then select Run recognition, and confirm.

18
00:00:59,057 --> 00:01:03,021
Ten journals are posted, and nothing is
waiting any more.

19
00:01:03,021 --> 00:01:05,795
Running it again is safe: a month

20
00:01:05,795 --> 00:01:08,173
already posted is never posted twice.

21
00:01:08,173 --> 00:01:12,137
Back on Fatima's contract, September is
Posted, with its journal.

22
00:01:12,137 --> 00:01:16,100
Open it: Advance Rent is debited 5,095.89,
the rent for

23
00:01:16,100 --> 00:01:20,064
September's thirty days, and Rental Income
is credited the same.
